Besides, what can I say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:31.440
if China, Russia or Pakistan were to recognize the&nbsp;
Taliban government, it would not be a surprise.
 &nbsp;

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:35.100
And so they have already taken some&nbsp;
steps in that direction: that of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:39.600
recognizing the Taliban. Of course, without&nbsp;
credible guarantees of security and cooperation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:43.680
this is also up in the air. And the truth is that&nbsp;
it would not change anything that much either.
 &nbsp;

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:53.400
It would be a different story if the United States&nbsp;
or the European Union were to recognize them. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:58.740
believe it or not, many US analysts are already&nbsp;
asking for it. The reason? Well, the usual one:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:03.180
to be able to influence to some extent the drift&nbsp;
of the Taliban government and the country.
 &nbsp;

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.980
("The United States should diplomatically&nbsp;
recognize Afghanistan's Taliban government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:12.120
This is not easy for (me) to say as a&nbsp;
former Afghan ambassador (...). Doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:16.260
so will be perceived as a painful betrayal&nbsp;
for many, but the alternative – allowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:21.060
Afghanistan's dangerous descent into a hermit&nbsp;
kingdom and forsaking the insight and means to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:26.640
influence or shape events – would mean more dire&nbsp;
consequences for all" – Javid Ahmed, former Afghan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:32.580
ambassador in a Foreign Policy article, 2023)
 
Like this ambassador, many analysts believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:37.620
neither sanctions nor any other form of coercion&nbsp;
is going to make the Taliban relent in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:41.280
efforts to continue violating human rights,&nbsp;
and that the best thing the United States can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:45.780
do at this point is to recognize this before&nbsp;
any other country does in an attempt to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:49.860
Afghanistan a less hostile place.
 
So this is the current debate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:59.400
In any case, for this to happen, there would first&nbsp;
have to be some certainty that the Taliban would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:04.380
listen to US recommendations, something that,&nbsp;
let's not kid ourselves, seems highly unlikely.
 &nbsp;

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.560
So far, Biden has given no sign&nbsp;
that he will recognize the Taliban,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:12.000
which is a blow to an Afghanistan that is going&nbsp;
through one of the worst times in its history.
 &nbsp;

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:17.640
That said the question is for all of you: do you&nbsp;
think Biden should recognize the Taliban? Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:22.320
Trump do so if he returned to the presidency&nbsp;
in 2024? Which State do you think will be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:26.220
first to recognize them? Will Russia be the&nbsp;
first to form a brotherhood of pariah States?

